<body>
<main data-frwd-document="">
<article data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002">
<h1 data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003">Rich components</h1>
<p data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004">Every component below reads correctly with no script running at all. The runtime adds behaviour on top; it never supplies the content.</p>

<frwd-callout data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005">
<aside data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006" class="frwd-callout">
<p data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007">A callout is ordinary complementary content, styled. No custom element is required for it to mean something.</p>
</aside>
</frwd-callout>

<frwd-disclosure data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008" data-frwd-expanded="false">
<button aria-expanded="false" data-frwd-disclosure-toggle="" type="button">Method notes</button>
<div data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009" data-frwd-disclosure-body="">
<p data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010">Collapsed detail that must still reach a printed page, because a reader holding paper cannot expand anything.</p>
</div>
</frwd-disclosure>

<details data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011">
<summary>Native disclosure</summary>
<span>Standard details and summary, used where they already solve the problem. Convenience content only: no block object, so nothing is lost if a printout omits it.</span>
</details>

<frwd-chart data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013" data-source="quarterly-revenue" data-type="bar" data-x="quarter" data-y="revenue">
<figure data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014">
<img alt="Revenue rose from ten in the first quarter to thirteen in the second." height="1" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk+M9QDwADhgGAWjR9awAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==" width="1">
<figcaption data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015">Quarterly revenue. The static figure is the baseline; the runtime may hydrate it later.</figcaption>
</figure>
</frwd-chart>

<p data-frwd-id="d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000016">Ordinary prose continues after the components, and reflows around them.</p>
</article>
</main>

</body></html>